  <content>
  <section><figure><media alt="Los Angeles county fair."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/e8b47724f5f8ec17be0e61287de32802b99adc9a"/></media></figure><newline/><para>For numbers 1 – 7, use the equation \(x + y = 20\) which represents the relationship between the number of games, \(x\), the number of rides, \(y\), and the dollar amount a student is spending on games and rides at an amusement park.</para>
<!--START QUESTION 1-->
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="33a13b30-322b-42d7-bc20-e13bbbc75e7c"><problem><para>
      <para>What’s the number of rides the student could get on if they don’t play any games?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>20</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 20. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!--START QUESTION 2-->
