  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
      <para>\((20,.0)\).</para>
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
      <para>Decreases by 1</para>
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
      <para>\((0,20)\).</para>
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
      <para>\(y = -x + 20\) or \(y = 20 -x\)</para>
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
      <para>The new equation shows where the graph intersects the \(y\)-axis at 20, so if the student plays 0 games, they have the money to go on 20 rides. Since the slope of the graph is \(-1\), for every 1 fewer ride they go on, they can play 1 game.</para>
